{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Google Colab Setup with GitHub Copilot\n","\n","In this notebook, we'll walk you through the setup of Google Colab and how to integrate it with GitHub Copilot for enhanced coding experience.\n","\n","## 1. Introduction\n","Google Colab is a powerful Jupyter notebook environment that runs in the cloud and offers free access to powerful machine learning and data analysis resources.\n","\n","## 2. Setting up Google Colab\n","To get started with Google Colab:\n","- Go to [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/)\n","- Sign in with your Google account.\n","- Create a new notebook or upload an existing one.\n","\n","## 3. Enabling GitHub Copilot\n","To enable GitHub Copilot in Google Colab:\n","- Install the VSCode integration for GitHub Copilot.\n","- Open your Colab notebook.\n","- Start coding, and Copilot will suggest code completions.\n","\n","## 4. Example Usage\n","```python\n","# Example code to demonstrate Copilot suggestions\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","def calculate_mean(data):\n","    return np.mean(data)\n","\n","# Let's test the function\n","test_data = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n","mean_value = calculate_mean(test_data)\n","print(f'Average: {mean_value}')\n","```"]}]}